#: ../../src/guide/introduction.rst:2
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "介绍"

#: ../../src/guide/introduction.rst:4
msgid ""
"This 'book' is a small set of tutorials about using libuv_ as a high "
"performance evented I/O library which offers the same API on Windows and "
"Unix."
msgstr "这本“书”是一小组教程，讲解如何将 libuv_ 用作一个高性能的事件驱动 I/O 库，它在 Windows 和 Unix 上提供相同的 API。"

#: ../../src/guide/introduction.rst:7
msgid ""
"It is meant to cover the main areas of libuv, but is not a comprehensive "
"reference discussing every function and data structure. The `official "
"libuv documentation`_ may be consulted for full details."
msgstr "它旨在涵盖 libuv 的主要领域，但并不是一部讨论每个函数和数据结构的详尽参考手册。完整细节可查阅 `official libuv documentation`_。"

#: ../../src/guide/introduction.rst:13
msgid ""
"This book is still a work in progress, so sections may be incomplete, but"
" I hope you will enjoy it as it grows."
msgstr "本书仍在编写之中，因此部分章节可能不完整，但希望随着它的成长，你会喜欢它。"

#: ../../src/guide/introduction.rst:17
msgid "Who this book is for"
msgstr "本书的目标读者"

#: ../../src/guide/introduction.rst:19
msgid "If you are reading this book, you are either:"
msgstr "如果你正在阅读本书，那么你属于以下二者之一："

#: ../../src/guide/introduction.rst:21
msgid ""
"a systems programmer, creating low-level programs such as daemons or "
"network services and clients. You have found that the event loop approach"
" is well suited for your application and decided to use libuv."
msgstr "系统程序员，编写守护进程或网络服务与客户端等底层程序。你已经发现事件循环的方式非常适合你的应用程序，并决定使用 libuv。"

#: ../../src/guide/introduction.rst:25
msgid ""
"a node.js module writer, who wants to wrap platform APIs written in C or "
"C++ with a set of (a)synchronous APIs that are exposed to JavaScript. You"
" will use libuv purely in the context of node.js. For this you will "
"require some other resources as the book does not cover parts specific to"
" v8/node.js."
msgstr "node.js 模块作者，希望用一组暴露给 JavaScript 的（非）同步 API 来包装以 C 或 C++ 编写的平台 API。你将纯粹在 node.js 的语境中使用 libuv。为此你还需要一些其他资源，因为本书不涵盖 v8/node.js 特有的内容。"

#: ../../src/guide/introduction.rst:31
msgid ""
"This book assumes that you are comfortable with the C programming "
"language."
msgstr "本书假定你对 C 编程语言已经相当熟悉。"

#: ../../src/guide/introduction.rst:34
msgid "Background"
msgstr "背景"

#: ../../src/guide/introduction.rst:36
msgid ""
"The node.js_ project began in 2009 as a JavaScript environment decoupled "
"from the browser. Using Google's V8_ and Marc Lehmann's libev_, node.js "
"combined a model of I/O -- evented -- with a language that was well "
"suited to the style of programming; due to the way it had been shaped by "
"browsers. As node.js grew in popularity, it was important to make it work"
" on Windows, but libev ran only on Unix. The Windows equivalent of kernel"
" event notification mechanisms like kqueue or (e)poll is IOCP. libuv was "
"an abstraction around libev or IOCP depending on the platform, providing "
"users an API based on libev. In the node-v0.9.0 version of libuv `libev "
"was removed`_."
msgstr "node.js_ 项目始于 2009 年，最初是一个与浏览器解耦的 JavaScript 环境。借助 Google 的 V8_ 与 Marc Lehmann 的 libev_，node.js 将 I/O 模型——事件驱动——与一门非常适合这种编程风格的语言结合了起来；这得益于该语言此前被浏览器塑造的方式。随着 node.js 日渐流行，让它能在 Windows 上运行变得十分重要，但 libev 只能运行在 Unix 上。Windows 上与 kqueue 或 (e)poll 这类内核事件通知机制相对应的是 IOCP。libuv 在当时是对 libev 或 IOCP 的抽象，具体取决于所在平台，并为用户提供基于 libev 的 API。在 libuv 的 node-v0.9.0 版本中，`libev was removed`_。"

#: ../../src/guide/introduction.rst:46
msgid ""
"Since then libuv has continued to mature and become a high quality "
"standalone library for system programming. Users outside of node.js "
"include Mozilla's Rust_ programming language, and a variety_ of language "
"bindings."
msgstr "从那以后，libuv 持续走向成熟，成为了一个用于系统编程的高质量独立库。node.js 之外的使用者包括 Mozilla 的 Rust_ 编程语言，以及 variety_ 的各种语言绑定。"

#: ../../src/guide/introduction.rst:50
msgid "This book and the code is based on libuv version `v1.42.0`_."
msgstr "本书及书中的代码基于 libuv 的 `v1.42.0`_ 版本。"

#: ../../src/guide/introduction.rst:53
msgid "Code"
msgstr "代码"

#: ../../src/guide/introduction.rst:55
msgid ""
"All the example code and the source of the book is included as part of "
"the libuv_ project on GitHub. Clone or Download libuv_, then build it::"
msgstr "所有示例代码和本书的源码都包含在 GitHub 上的 libuv_ 项目中。克隆或下载 libuv_，然后构建它："

#: ../../src/guide/introduction.rst:63
msgid ""
"There is no need to ``make install``. To build the examples run ``make`` "
"in the ``docs/code/`` directory."
msgstr "无需执行 ``make install``。要构建示例，请运行 ``make``，该命令需在 ``docs/code/`` 目录中执行。"

